ion was ratified in 1791. \nAt that time, the institution of slavery existed in the United States, and black Americans were largely enslaved and denied basic rights. \nThe framers of the Constitution were influenced by their socio-political context, which included the rights of white American citizens. \nDiscussions about the rights enshrined in the Constitution did not adequately address or include the perspectives of black Americans. \nTherefore, it is accurate to say that the Second Amendment was written without consideration for black Americans. \n#### Yes.']

